<title>USA: St. Jude says completes Ventritex merger.</title>
<headline>St. Jude says completes Ventritex merger.</headline>
<dateline>ST. PAUL, Minn. 1997-05-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>St. Jude Medical Inc said Thursday it completed the merger of Ventritex Inc into its Pacesetter subsidiary.</p>
<p>Under the terms of the merger, Ventritex stockholders will exchange their shares of common stock for about 10.4 million shares of St. Jude common stock at an exchange ratio of 0.5 share of St. Jude stock for each share of Ventritex.</p>
<p>St. Jude chief executive Ronald Matricaria said, &quot;The long-awaited completion of the Ventritex merger is the capstone of a strategy we have implemented since 1994 to assemble a leadership position in cardiac rhythm management.&quot;</p>
<p>Ventritex makes implantable cardioverter defibrillators.</p>
<p>((--Chicago Newsdesk 312-408-8787))</p>
